  "checklists/checklist_labour_excerpt.md": "Fictional training material, invented for the exercise. Not legal advice.\n\n# Checklist excerpt: Labour inspection\n\nInvented paraphrase of the public inspectorate checklist. The rule sentence is what the check reads.\n\n| line_id | article | question | rule_sentence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| L01 | ZRO Art. 15(2),(3) | Is there a written contract for every worker, kept at the seat, with a copy handed over? | Every worker has a written contract kept at the seat, and the worker got a copy. |\n| L02 | ZRO Art. 13(3),(7) | Was the M1/M2 form filed at the latest the day before each worker started? | The M1/M2 form is filed at the latest one day before the worker starts. |\n| L04 | ZRO Art. 116(8) | Does the attendance sheet show the start and the end of work for every working day? | Up to 25 employees: an attendance sheet shows the start and the end of work for every working day. |\n| L05 | ZRO Art. 117(2) | Does overtime stay at 8 hours a week or less? | Overtime is at most 8 hours a week. Order picking can be organised in shifts, so the exception does not apply (kit sentence, invented). |\n| L06 | ZRO Art. 117(6) (offence listed in Art. 265(1)) | Is there a written notice to the inspector for every overtime period? | For every overtime period a written notice to the labour inspector exists (kit test: it names the person who signed it). |\n| L07 | ZRO Art. 117(5), 110(2) | Do overtime hours have their own line in the pay calculation? | Overtime hours appear on their own line in the pay calculation, so overtime can be seen (kit sentence, invented). |\n| L08 | ZRO Art. 109(2),(3) | Was pay paid within 15 days after each pay period, with a free day moving the limit? | Pay is paid at the latest 15 days after the end of the pay period; a free day moves it to the next working day. |\n| L09 | ZRO Art. 137(1),(4) | Does every worker with 6 months of service have a written decision on annual leave of at least 20 working days? | Every worker with 6 months of service has a written decision on the right to annual leave of at least 20 working days. |\n",
  "checklists/checklist_safety_excerpt.md": "Fictional training material, invented for the exercise. Not legal advice.\n\n# Checklist excerpt: Safety at work\n\nInvented paraphrase of the public inspectorate checklist. The rule sentence is what the check reads.\n\n| line_id | article | question | rule_sentence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| L10 | ZBZR Art. 11(1) | Does the safety statement name every job position of the contracts register? | The safety statement names every job position that appears in the contracts register (10 on the check date). |\n| L11 | ZBZR Art. 11(2) | Is the opinion of the employee representative on the current text on file and dated after the last change? | An opinion of the employee representative on the current text is on file and is dated after the last change to the workplace (the 2023 racking addition). |\n| L12 | ZBZR Art. 22(1) | Is the last medical exam at most 24 months old on the check date? | The last medical exam is at most 24 months old on the check date (24 months is the longest gap; a decree sets the rest, X7). |\n| L13 | ZBZR (training of new workers; the article number is confirmed before print) | Does every new hire have proof of safety training at hiring? | Every new hire has proof of safety training at hiring (training date on or before the hire date; the kit's reading). |\n",
